# CRITICAL CHECKPOINT: Documentation Workflow

## TRIGGER
When making any changes to the codebase

## ENFORCEMENT
Must check and update project management documentation

## WORKFLOW STEPS

### 1. Before Making Changes
- **ALWAYS check project-mgmt documentation first**
  - Read `shared/docs/project-mgmt/README.md` for current status
  - Check relevant implementation plan documents
  - Verify current status assessment matches reality
  - Identify any discrepancies between docs and code

### 2. During Implementation
- **Update status as you work**
  - Mark completed tasks as ✅
  - Update partially implemented as ⏳
  - Remove completed items from "Critical Missing"
  - Add new discoveries to appropriate sections

### 3. After Completing Changes
- **Update all relevant documents**
  - Update status assessments in all affected documents
  - Remove completed tasks from pending lists
  - Add new tasks discovered during implementation
  - Update file references to match actual implementation

## DOCUMENT UPDATE PATTERNS

### Status Updates
- **✅ Completed**: Move from "Critical Missing" or "Partially Implemented"
- **⏳ Partially Implemented**: Update when basic structure exists but logic missing
- **❌ Critical Missing**: Add new discoveries or move from completed

### File Reference Updates
- **Current Working Files**: Add new files you create
- **Missing Implementation Files**: Remove files you implement, add new discoveries
- **Key Files for Implementation**: Update with actual file paths

## VALIDATION CHECKLIST
- [ ] Checked project-mgmt README for current status
- [ ] Referenced relevant implementation plan documents
- [ ] Updated status assessments in affected documents
- [ ] Updated file references to match implementation
- [ ] Removed completed tasks from pending lists
- [ ] Added new discoveries to appropriate sections
- [ ] Verified documentation accuracy after changes

## CONSEQUENCES OF VIOLATIONS
- **Inconsistent documentation** - docs don't match reality
- **Lost context** - future work based on outdated info
- **Duplicated effort** - re-implementing already done work
- **Project confusion** - unclear what's actually implemented

## EXAMPLES

### ✅ CORRECT - Update Documentation
```markdown
### ✅ Completed (60% of core functionality)
- **Formula System**: Enhanced implementation with FeatureModifierFormulaParams
- **Formula Preview UI**: Dynamic preview showing actual progression patterns
```

### ❌ WRONG - Ignore Documentation
```typescript
// Making changes without checking or updating docs
// This leads to inconsistent project state
```

## WHY THIS RULE EXISTS
- **Project management docs are living documents** - they must reflect current reality
- **Documentation accuracy is more important than implementation speed**
- **When in doubt, update the docs first**
- **Effective AI agent collaboration requires accurate documentation**

